\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Field Citation Ratio (FCR) expresses the citation-based impact of the publication set relative to publications from the same research area and year. FCR=1 implies that publications are cited as often as expected based on publication year and research area. FCR=2 implies that publications are cited twice as often as expected based on publication year and research area. \textbf  {Note:} References to datasets are counted here as ``Publications with FCR", which are rarely cited in publications. The FCR values from peer-reviewed publications only are therefore higher than the FCR values reported here. (\emph  {Date: July 29, 2026})}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
